The sequence $x_n$ converges to $c$ in $\ell_1$, meaning $\|x_n - c\|_1 \to 0$. For any $p > 1$, we use the inequality $\|x\|_p \leq \|x\|_1$ for all $x \in \ell_1$. This inequality holds because each term $|x_k|^p \leq |x_k| \cdot \|x\|_1^{p-1}$, leading to $\|x\|_p^p \leq \|x\|_1^p$. Thus, $\|x_n - c\|_p \leq \|x_n - c\|_1 \to 0$, proving convergence in $\ell_p$.

**Final Answer**
\boxed{\text{Yes}}

